    "hash": "hq9nzkr8GLvUuGBdJ1DJvesa1Ns=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:07.992Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Senacor Technologies is a custom-development firm working banking, insurance and logistics, and the research reads it as a likely Camunda partner that nobody has checked. The Camunda attribution is unverified; the reason to expect it to hold is that German Camunda density is high and Senacor sits in the sectors where that density concentrates.\n\nA custom-development core is the second signal. A firm whose business is bespoke build has no product of its own competing for the application layer, so if the Camunda footprint turns out to be real, both halves of the cohort thesis apply to the same lead at once.\n\nThe actionable content of this note is the gap rather than the firm: this is a plausible fit sitting at priority 3 purely because nobody has yet spent the time it would take to confirm the tooling.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Senacor Technologies (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Custom development core, banking/insurance/logistics. German Camunda density is high - a likely partner nobody has checked.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:07.992526Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:07.992530Z"
    }
  },
